      "SearchMode": {
        "description": "Which retriever answers a query.\n\nThey fail in opposite directions \u2014 the vector half is blind to opaque exact\ntokens, the keyword half is blind to paraphrase \u2014 and M2.1 measured that\ncomplement before M2.2 fused it, so that it was possible to tell which half\ncarries which query. `SKIP LOCKED` goes from recall 0.000 to 1.000 between\nthem; the paraphrase queries go the other way, to exactly 0.000.\n\n`HYBRID` is the product. The other two remain because the only way to know\nwhat fusion is doing is to be able to run each half alone.",
        "enum": [
          "vector",
          "keyword",
          "hybrid"
        ],
        "title": "SearchMode",
        "type": "string"
      },
